## [e13c] order of after-commit callbacks (registered: PlainSync, AnnotatedSync, OverrideSync, then publishEvent -> listeners first, second)
getSynchronizations() just before commit, inside the transaction:
  sorted[0] OverrideSync [getOrder() = 0]  getOrder()=0
  sorted[1] TransactionalApplicationListenerSynchronization$PlatformSynchronization  getOrder()=1
  sorted[2] PlainSync [no order]  getOrder()=LOWEST_PRECEDENCE
  sorted[3] AnnotatedSync [@Order(0) on class]  getOrder()=LOWEST_PRECEDENCE
  sorted[4] TransactionalApplicationListenerSynchronization$PlatformSynchronization  getOrder()=LOWEST_PRECEDENCE
actual call order after commit:
  1. afterCommit()      OverrideSync [getOrder() = 0]
  2. afterCommit()      PlainSync [no order]
  3. afterCommit()      AnnotatedSync [@Order(0) on class]
  4. afterCompletion()  OverrideSync [getOrder() = 0] (status=COMMITTED)
  5. AFTER_COMMIT listener  first [@Order(1) on method]
  6. afterCompletion()  PlainSync [no order] (status=COMMITTED)
  7. afterCompletion()  AnnotatedSync [@Order(0) on class] (status=COMMITTED)
  8. AFTER_COMMIT listener  second [no @Order]
